4570
04:57:43,370 --> 04:57:49,950
If I just walk around in circles with no sound, people are gonna think, what the fuck are you doing?

4571
04:57:51,950 --> 04:57:52,890
That's the worst.

4572
04:57:53,550 --> 04:57:54,130
Nah, man.

4573
04:57:54,590 --> 04:57:55,430
That's not good.

4574
04:58:00,700 --> 04:58:05,960
I can't wait for 60 years from now and we're all still watching Oliver stream games as an actual dementia bitch.

4575
04:58:06,320 --> 04:58:10,560
Guys, there's one good thing about maybe getting dementia later.

4576
04:58:10,800 --> 04:58:13,840
I can forget about certain games that I love and play them again.

4577
04:58:15,340 --> 04:58:16,920
Wouldn't it be fucking hilarious?

4578
04:58:17,240 --> 04:58:19,880
I mean, let's not hope I actually get to suffer from something.

4579
04:58:20,360 --> 04:58:26,320
But imagine if I do end up suffering from something, I lose my memory for whatever reason.

4580
04:58:26,420 --> 04:58:28,340
Maybe I have a... I don't know, I fall on my bike.

4581
04:58:28,780 --> 04:58:36,380
You know, I lose my memories, and I do a second Outer Wilds, and it's like, it's getting more popular than the first.

4582
04:58:37,040 --> 04:58:37,960
Imagine that!

4583
04:58:38,820 --> 04:58:41,940
That would be insane content, actually.

4584
04:58:43,360 --> 04:58:48,500
The title would be, I lost my memory and I played Outer Wilds blind.

4585
04:58:49,460 --> 04:58:50,680
That would be insane.

4586
04:58:54,460 --> 04:58:57,660
If I do have dementia, damn right I'm gonna monetize it.

4587
04:59:00,420 --> 04:59:04,800
Oh man.

4588
04:59:06,220 --> 04:59:07,180
Holy shit.

4589
04:59:08,840 --> 04:59:11,560
I mean, obviously I would watch all the shows that I love.

4590
04:59:12,020 --> 04:59:14,020
But then again, I wouldn't know that I loved them.

4591
04:59:14,940 --> 04:59:16,680
Oh man, what a conundrum.

4592
04:59:23,290 --> 04:59:23,970
Amnesia stream.

4593
04:59:27,810 --> 04:59:28,990
I need to write them down.

4594
04:59:29,270 --> 04:59:30,430
Yeah, that's a good idea.

4595
04:59:31,050 --> 04:59:34,730
I've heard writing things down in general is a good idea when you're suffering from memory issues.

4596
04:59:43,680 --> 04:59:45,880
All the space information might jog your memory?

4597
04:59:48,480 --> 04:59:49,140
Probably, yeah.

4598
04:59:51,180 --> 04:59:53,200
Like, I still remember most of Outer Wilds.

4599
04:59:53,260 --> 04:59:54,420
It's not like I forget any of it.

4600
04:59:55,380 --> 04:59:58,800
If you ask me now, I could tell you pretty much anything about that game, I think.

4601
05:00:09,780 --> 05:00:11,040
I always forget to write.

4602
05:00:11,220 --> 05:00:13,280
When I'm trying to write something, I'm trying not to forget.

4603
05:00:14,840 --> 05:00:19,820
Yeah, because your mind goes, I'll remember to write that down later, or I'll remember that one for sure, right?

4604
05:00:19,900 --> 05:00:20,580
So you skip it.

4605
05:00:20,960 --> 05:00:22,740
But you know you're not going to be able to remember it.

4606
05:00:22,900 --> 05:00:23,880
It's the worst mistake.

4607
05:00:27,390 --> 05:00:29,190
How do you get to the Southern Observatory?

4608
05:00:29,890 --> 05:00:30,590
Very easy.

4609
05:00:31,590 --> 05:00:33,370
Spoilers here for Outer Wilds.

4610
05:00:33,730 --> 05:00:37,530
So if you haven't played that game, put me on mute for like 51 seconds.

4611
05:00:37,990 --> 05:00:39,310
Starting now.

4612
05:00:39,850 --> 05:00:44,750
In order to get to the Southern Observatory, you are going to go to Ryback.

4613
05:00:45,090 --> 05:00:48,730
And he is on that planet with the black hole.

4614
05:00:48,890 --> 05:00:49,630
Okay, you go in there.

4615
05:00:49,930 --> 05:00:51,710
You have to follow the gravity crystals.

4616
05:00:51,710 --> 05:00:52,690
You walk upside down.

4617
05:00:52,810 --> 05:00:53,450
You have to do a jump.

4618
05:00:53,530 --> 05:00:54,590
Then you get to sort of a...

4619
05:00:55,070 --> 05:00:59,430
Some kind of a ruin where you jump up through the ruin and then, you know, you do a certain thing and then you're there.

4620
05:00:59,750 --> 05:01:00,250
Did I get it right?

4621
05:01:00,890 --> 05:01:01,950
And you follow the signs.

4622
05:01:02,430 --> 05:01:02,790
Boom.

4623
05:01:03,570 --> 05:01:04,170
There it is.

4624
05:01:05,570 --> 05:01:05,930
See?

4625
05:01:06,410 --> 05:01:07,350
I remember everything.

4626
05:01:09,970 --> 05:01:17,750
Also, uh... I'm gonna say... I don't think this Southern Observatory was as big of a meme as you guys make it out to be.

4627
05:01:18,610 --> 05:01:19,690
Like, to this day.

4628
05:01:20,230 --> 05:01:23,650
People keep commenting on every single game I'm playing.

4629
05:01:24,310 --> 05:01:26,390
X is the new Southern Observatory.

4630
05:01:26,710 --> 05:01:28,010
What are you talking about?

4631
05:01:28,230 --> 05:01:30,290
I feel like I nailed the Southern Observatory.

4632
05:01:30,810 --> 05:01:33,150
Yeah, like, I fell down a couple times, right?

4633
05:01:33,210 --> 05:01:35,710
But I know exactly... Like, I feel like I nailed it.

4634
05:01:36,290 --> 05:01:36,930
Didn't I?

4635
05:01:41,690 --> 05:01:43,030
The Subnautica radio?

4636
05:01:45,650 --> 05:01:46,950
Here's the crazy thing, okay?

4637
05:01:47,110 --> 05:01:52,210
I'm gonna talk to you guys about the disconnect between the streamer and the viewer here, okay?

4638
05:01:53,150 --> 05:01:57,630
So, for example, when it came to Subnautica, alright?

4639
05:01:59,290 --> 05:02:03,310
Like, when I was playing, I did not forget about the radio.

4640
05:02:04,390 --> 05:02:04,830
Ever.

4641
05:02:05,710 --> 05:02:08,070
Like, I saw the icon, you know, on the right side.

4642
05:02:08,310 --> 05:02:10,070
I just don't comment on it.

4643
05:02:10,770 --> 05:02:12,490
I knew it was there, but I...

4644
05:02:12,520 --> 05:02:16,220
Intentionally delayed it because I wanted to do other things first, right?

4645
05:02:16,880 --> 05:02:26,220
And people kept commenting, oh, you don't trust the developers... You should totally trust the developers to provide a good, you know, flow of the game.

4646
05:02:28,080 --> 05:02:35,400
And the answer to that is, well, I trust the developers so much that there's still a good flow to the game even if I don't activate the radio early.

4647
05:02:35,780 --> 05:02:36,560
And you know what?

4648
05:02:36,680 --> 05:02:38,660
Everything was fine, as it turns out.

4649
05:02:38,840 --> 05:02:39,720
Nothing ever went wrong.

4650
05:02:39,720 --> 05:02:40,460
It was great.

4651
05:02:44,510 --> 05:02:53,030
But I gotta say, though, the last episode, before I actually clicked on the radio, it did occur to me at that moment that people were commenting a lot about it.

4652
05:02:53,990 --> 05:02:57,170
So I may or may not have teased you a little bit in that last episode.

4653
05:03:01,210 --> 05:03:02,770
I had so much fun with that, actually.

4654
05:03:05,800 --> 05:03:10,680
I felt like delaying it even more just because people commented about it.

4655
05:03:13,440 --> 05:03:14,640
Which one was that episode?

4656
05:03:14,760 --> 05:03:15,440
Episode 16.

4657
05:03:16,220 --> 05:03:21,680
And the reason I remember that is because I remember answering a comment.

4658
05:03:22,400 --> 05:03:28,640
Someone was on, like, I think episode 7, and they were like, oh god, tell me he activates the radio soon, or something, right?

4659
05:03:29,480 --> 05:03:30,960
And that was on episode 7.

4660
05:03:31,430 --> 05:03:34,490
And at that point, I already had episodes up to 16 and all that.

4661
05:03:35,530 --> 05:03:38,670
And I knew it happened there, because I made the meme in that video, right?

4662
05:03:38,750 --> 05:03:40,170
So it was still fresh in my memory.

4663
05:03:40,430 --> 05:03:44,790
And I answered back something like, get ready to wait for a while, you know?

4664
05:03:45,130 --> 05:03:45,890
Something like that.

4665
05:03:49,650 --> 05:03:52,710
Your song title choices in the Subnautica series are so good, by the way.

4666
05:03:53,410 --> 05:03:54,330
Hey, I'm glad you like them.

4667
05:03:54,430 --> 05:03:55,790
Underwater Love became one of my favorites.

4668
05:03:55,950 --> 05:03:56,590
It's such a good one.

4669
05:03:56,710 --> 05:03:57,490
I love that song.

4670
05:03:59,390 --> 05:04:07,150
Yeah, for those that don't know, all the titles of the Subnautica 1 and the expansion videos, all of them, are titles of songs that I really enjoy.

4671
05:04:07,750 --> 05:04:13,810
And those titles are also kind of relevant to what happens in the actual... in the episode, right?

4672
05:04:14,350 --> 05:04:15,950
I don't know, I thought that was fun to do at the time.

4673
05:04:17,550 --> 05:04:19,810
They're all for my Spotify playlist, pretty much.

4674
05:04:23,380 --> 05:04:27,980
I was low-key hoping you would already use the Minecraft remixes for your pre-streamed title screen.

4675
05:04:29,200 --> 05:04:31,700
Uh, am I even allowed to stream those songs?

4676
05:04:32,880 --> 05:04:34,560
They're not officially in any game, right?

4677
05:04:34,620 --> 05:04:35,840
It's not a video game soundtrack?

4678
05:04:36,760 --> 05:04:38,320
I'm not sure I can put that on YouTube.

4679
05:04:46,400 --> 05:04:47,740
How do we recommend music?

4680
05:04:47,860 --> 05:04:48,260
What do you mean?

4681
05:04:54,400 --> 05:04:59,200
I mean, what I can do is I can put it in a video and just upload it as unlisted and see if there's an issue.

4682
05:05:01,960 --> 05:05:02,740
But it would be cool.

4683
05:05:03,020 --> 05:05:04,100
I'm gonna check it out for sure.

4684
05:05:09,120 --> 05:05:12,140
Maybe the real Southern Observatory was the friends we made along the way?

4685
05:05:12,380 --> 05:05:12,840
You know what?

4686
05:05:12,860 --> 05:05:13,700
What's funny, Teflon?

4687
05:05:13,860 --> 05:05:15,680
That exact comment you just made there?

4688
05:05:17,080 --> 05:05:20,460
Many people have said that exact same thing, and it's always funny.

4689
05:05:20,860 --> 05:05:22,620
I don't know, it just gets me.

4690
05:05:24,280 --> 05:05:26,220
It's a very common saying around here.

4691
05:05:27,640 --> 05:05:28,720
You just need to credit?

4692
05:05:28,940 --> 05:05:29,380
Yeah, I figured.

4693
05:05:29,540 --> 05:05:34,260
Okay, so if it's Andrew Prowlow, I don't know what his stance is on that.

4694
05:05:36,960 --> 05:05:38,840
I'm never letting pluck the whole meme die.

4695
05:05:40,260 --> 05:05:41,460
Yeah, that was a meme for a while.

4696
05:05:41,600 --> 05:05:42,640
It's not much of a meme anymore.

4697
05:05:52,230 --> 05:05:53,830
Play Tekken 5 music?

4698
05:05:54,250 --> 05:05:54,650
Unforgiven?

4699
05:05:56,870 --> 05:05:58,890
I used to play Tekken when I was a child.

4700
05:05:59,030 --> 05:06:00,910
I forgot which one, but on the PlayStation, I think.

4701
05:06:01,930 --> 05:06:03,330
I was never very good at it.

4702
05:06:03,410 --> 05:06:04,810
I'm not a big fan of fighting games.

4703
05:06:06,690 --> 05:06:08,310
It's commissioned music by Minecraft.

4704
05:06:08,310 --> 05:06:09,290
They hold the copyright.

4705
05:06:12,770 --> 05:06:15,350
Yeah, I don't know the copyright laws when it comes to remixes.

4706
05:06:17,630 --> 05:06:18,570
Let me ask you something.

4707
05:06:18,710 --> 05:06:26,830
If I were to take the instrumental of a very known song and just sing along to it myself, that's not considered a remix, right?

4708
05:06:26,910 --> 05:06:28,930
That's more like a cover, I guess?

4709
05:06:29,550 --> 05:06:31,950
But I'm using the instrumental of the original song.

4710
05:06:32,070 --> 05:06:32,650
Is that a problem?

4711
05:06:33,590 --> 05:06:34,410
Because I don't know.

4712
05:06:47,320 --> 05:06:49,000
You should totally play it first.

4713
05:06:49,540 --> 05:06:49,940
Always.

4714
05:06:50,860 --> 05:06:53,520
I mean... That's just my opinion, right?

4715
05:06:53,680 --> 05:06:57,660
But if you're not into the whole scary parts of it and you don't want to play it yourself, I understand.

4716
05:06:59,040 --> 05:07:03,580
But in general, I would say always play it first if it's anything you think is interesting.

4717
05:07:04,520 --> 05:07:07,080
If it's not your cup of tea, then maybe not, you know?

4718
05:07:12,880 --> 05:07:14,700
Silly song cover for the intro song?

4719
05:07:14,860 --> 05:07:16,320
Yeah, that would be the perfect one, wouldn't it?

4720
05:07:16,640 --> 05:07:19,140
I totally have lyrics for that one already, by the way.

4721
05:07:20,000 --> 05:07:20,500
Okay.

4722
05:07:20,860 --> 05:07:22,240
I'm about to head on out of here.

4723
05:07:23,080 --> 05:07:25,920
And probably stream on Monday, I would say.

4724
05:07:26,200 --> 05:07:27,280
Either Monday or Tuesday.

4725
05:07:28,020 --> 05:07:29,860
One of those days, 100%.

4726
05:07:29,860 --> 05:07:31,800
Most likely Monday.

4727
05:07:32,600 --> 05:07:34,360
And thank you everyone for watching.

4728
05:07:35,320 --> 05:07:37,280
Minecraft is going strong.

4729
05:07:37,620 --> 05:07:39,960
It's crazy how much this game has...

4730
05:07:41,600 --> 05:07:43,020
Fucking changed my life, I guess.

4731
05:07:44,100 --> 05:07:44,760
Alright, goodnight.

4732
05:07:45,140 --> 05:07:46,240
Enjoy your weekend, okay?

4733
05:07:47,200 --> 05:07:47,940
I'll see you around.

4734
05:07:48,040 --> 05:07:48,260
Bye-bye.

